The inputs and outputs of the module that [[Approvals]] uses.

== Inputs ==
{| class="wikitable"
! Name !! Default !! Description
|-
| <code>repository</code> || || The repository whose workflow plans and applies.
|-
| <code>environments</code> || || One environment per workspace, named after it.
|-
| <code>auto_apply</code> || <code>[]</code> || Environments that apply without an approval, like HCP Terraform's auto apply. List the same workspaces in the action's <code>auto-apply</code> input.
|-
| <code>reviewer_teams</code> || <code>[]</code> || IDs of the teams whose approval starts an apply.
|-
| <code>reviewer_users</code> || <code>[]</code> || IDs of the users whose approval starts an apply.
|-
| <code>prevent_self_review</code> || <code>false</code> || Whether the person who pushed the change may approve its apply. Leave it off when one person does both.
|-
| <code>can_admins_bypass</code> || <code>false</code> || Whether repository administrators may start an apply without an approval.
|}

At least one reviewer team or user is required, unless every environment is in <code>auto_apply</code>.

== Outputs ==
{| class="wikitable"
! Name !! Description
|-
| <code>environments</code> || The environments, by workspace.
|}
